  "description": "Tree T001 - Sycamore (Category C) The proposed works comprise the removal of Sycamore Tree T001, an on-site Category C tree as identified in the submitted Arboricultural Impact Assessment. Tree T001 is a self-seeded sycamore located in immediate proximity to existing electrical substation infrastructure. Trees in such locations are generally discouraged due to operational and safety constraints, including potential conflicts with underground services, structural assets, and the requirement to maintain unrestricted access for inspection, maintenance, and emergency works. The site is underlain by shrinkable London Clay soils, and the continued presence of the tree presents an increased risk of soil movement associated with tree water demand, with the potential to adversely affect nearby infrastructure. The arboricultural assessment concludes that Tree T001 is of low to moderate quality, offers limited amenity or ecological value, and that its long-term retention is not appropriate given the constraints of its location. The removal of Tree T001 is therefore justified on arboricultural, engineering, and safety grounds. A separate full planning application for a residential development on the site is to be submitted in parallel. This tree works application is made independently and is supported by the arboricultural assessment, irrespective of the outcome of that application.",
